```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    usort($set, function ($a, $b) use ($order) {
        $ageA = $a['age'];
        $ageB = $b['age'];

        if ($ageA === $ageB) {
            return 0;
        }

        return $order ? $ageA < $ageB : $ageA > $ageB;
    });

    return $set;
}
```

The function uses PHP's built-in `usort()` function with a closure as the comparison callback. The comparison logic checks the ages of the two arrays and returns either 0 (if they're equal), or -1/1 depending on the value of the `$order` parameter (which should be passed from outside).

